{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Import

SSH keys can be imported using their ID:

```shell
terraform import dokploy_ssh_key.example efg123-sshkey-id
```

Or using import blocks (Terraform 1.5+):

```hcl
import {
  to = dokploy_ssh_key.example
  id = "efg123-sshkey-id"
}
```

### Finding SSH Key IDs

Use the `dokploy_ssh_keys` data source to discover SSH key IDs:

```hcl
data "dokploy_ssh_keys" "all" {}

output "ssh_key_ids" {
  value = { for k in data.dokploy_ssh_keys.all.ssh_keys : k.name => k.id }
}
```

~> **Note:** The `private_key` value will not be populated during import. You will need to set this value in your configuration after import if you want Terraform to manage it.
